Didier Stevens — 1768.py and cs-analyze-processdump.py
------------------------------------------------------

Description
  Cobalt Strike beacon configuration analysis and Sleep Mask XOR-key recovery.

Author
  Didier Stevens <https://blog.didierstevens.com/>

Sources
  https://github.com/DidierStevens/DidierStevensSuite/blob/master/1768.py
  https://github.com/DidierStevens/DidierStevensSuite/blob/master/cs-analyze-processdump.py

License
  Public Domain:
  "Source code put in the public domain by Didier Stevens, no Copyright"

Used in
  dumpex/hunt/cs_beacon/scanner.py
  dumpex/hunt/cs_beacon/parser.py
  dumpex/hunt/cs_beacon/schema.py
  dumpex/hunt/encoding/sleep_mask.py
  dumpex/rules_pkg/data/yara/cs_indicators.yar

Nature of use
  The beacon configuration candidate scan, TLV parser, field tables, Malleable
  C2 instruction decoder, version estimator, sanity checks, and XOR-encoded
  configuration markers are adapted from 1768.py.

  The 13-byte Sleep Mask XOR-key recovery approach and validation marker are
  adapted from cs-analyze-processdump.py. dumpex adds bounded scanning,
  coverage reporting, classification, and integration with its own hunt model.

  dumpex/hunt/cs_beacon/der.py adds full DER structure and length validation
  against the rsaEncryption OID; that hardening is original to dumpex rather
  than adapted from the simpler prefix check in 1768.py.


